# LF everywhere, on every checkout: shell scripts and hooks need it to run, and the C# formatting check (.editorconfig
# end_of_line = lf) would otherwise fail on a Windows checkout that converts to CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Except batch files, which players run with cmd.exe: Windows' own line endings, as Notepad shows them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# Generated sounds (#839) are bytes, compared exactly by their test: never converted.
*.wav binary
# The generated settings reference (tools/Metaphor.SettingsReference) is never merged by text (#892): a local merge keeps
# this side whole through the clone-local driver that scripts/setup/onboard.ps1 sets, and you regenerate the page after.
# GitHub's own merges ignore drivers; see "Stale settings reference" in docs/contributors/README.md for what to do then.
docs/players/reference/settings.md merge=settings-reference
